  "phrases": [
    {
      "id": "hook",
      "text": "That amazing old book smell is literally the smell of the book slowly breaking down.",
      "start": 0.077,
      "end": 4.47,
      "wordRange": [
        0,
        14
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "materials",
      "text": "As paper, ink, glue, and bindings age, they release volatile chemicals into the air.",
      "start": 4.81,
      "end": 9.657,
      "wordRange": [
        15,
        28
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "compounds",
      "text": "Different compounds can create grassy, musty, almond-like, and even vanilla-like smells.",
      "start": 9.978,
      "end": 15.118,
      "wordRange": [
        29,
        39
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "vanillin",
      "text": "Vanillin is one of the compounds associated with that familiar sweet note.",
      "start": 15.419,
      "end": 18.814,
      "wordRange": [
        40,
        51
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "science",
      "text": "Scientists and conservators can even study these emissions to learn about the condition of aging paper.",
      "start": 19.191,
      "end": 24.274,
      "wordRange": [
        52,
        67
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "payoff",
      "text": "So when Bill opens a 100-year-old book and thinks it smells weirdly delicious, he is basically enjoying the smell of chemistry happening in extremely slow motion.",
      "start": 24.642,
      "end": 33.111,
      "wordRange": [
        68,
        93
      ]
    }
  ],
